A||N||6||87ECO5||Putting a Microsoft Powerpoint Slide Presentation onto a VHS Tape||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||07-13-2001||01:21 PM||||My wife and I have been asked to create a powerpoint slide presentation, put it to music, then put it on a VHS tape.  We’ve scanned the pictures for the slide show and we’ve collected the MP3 files for the music, but we’re hitting a road block trying to find a way to put everything onto tape.<P>Are there places that rent equipment that can do this?  Are there places that will do it for you?<P>Is there anyone out there that has the necessary equipment that will accept money, a blank tape and our files, and do it for us?  We’re under a deadline.  We need to have this done by next weekend (7/22).<P>HELP!!!!!!!<P>TIA<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 07-13-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-13-2001||02:20 PM||||There are a few places that sell the equipment, that's only a few hundred dollars. it's a pretty simple setup, and you can get it at most places that sell computer equipment. I don't know what it was called though. Renting, however, I'm not sure about.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||07-13-2001||04:50 PM||||Go to BestBuy and buy a TV card and connect your VCR to it. That's what I do... The card I have is stereo and everything. Was about $150...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
